 R←Test_Table_002(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;Tbl;md
⍝ `GetTableRows` ignores neighbouring lines that are not table rows, even when there is no empty line in between
⍝ R gets one of: 0=Okay, 1=test case failed, ¯1=test case was not executed due to the "batchFlag"
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 Tbl←##.Meddy.Tables

 ⍝ A table inside a list: neither the list item nor the trailing note belong to it
 md←'* Item' '  | A | B |' '  |---|---|' '  | 1 | 2 |' '  a trailing note'
 →T.PassesIf 1 2 3≡Tbl.GetTableRows 2 md

 ⍝ Two tables separated by a line of prose must not be merged into one
 md←'| A | B |' '|---|---|' 'prose line' '| C | D |' '|---|---|'
 →T.PassesIf 0 1≡Tbl.GetTableRows 0 md
 →T.PassesIf 3 4≡Tbl.GetTableRows 3 md

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
